+7. Generate a single `FINAL_VERIFICATION_SUMMARY.md` with one row per command: exact command, working directory, dependency/environment version, exit code, result, log path, and commit/tree hash. Include pass/fail counts and skipped/blocked tests. Do not merge counts from separate test runs.
+8. Create `FINAL_TEST_MATRIX.json` with machine-readable status for every acceptance item: `PASS`, `FAIL`, `BLOCKED`, or `NOT RUN` and evidence path.
+9. Generate a SHA-256 manifest for the final source archive and all evidence files after the files are final. Verify the manifest once more after packaging.
+10. If a check cannot run due to unavailable network, browser, system dependency, or service, record the exact blocker and a command the developer can execute locally. Do not classify a blocked test as passed.
+
+## Frontend security/audit hygiene
+
+Review existing package audit findings. Do not run an unreviewed blanket upgrade. Record the affected package, severity, whether it is production/dev dependency, available fixed version within compatible ranges, and proposed remediation. Apply safe compatible fixes only when tests and lockfile remain consistent; otherwise report as a release blocker or documented deferral.
