+
+# 9. Final acceptance gate — C2 closure
+
+C2 may be reported as `PASS / CLOSED` only if **all mandatory items below pass** and the evidence points to the final source snapshot:
+
+- [ ] No unlabelled fixed `250000`-m² area assumptions remain in production-facing estimate/report/optimizer paths.
+- [ ] Selected study area drives the correct estimates; area/footprint/coverage definitions and units are consistent.
+- [ ] All thermal endpoints reject unsupported study-area IDs with HTTP 422 and have explicit regression tests.
+- [ ] Shareable archive contains no populated local database, credentials, `.env` secrets, or prohibited runtime artifacts; packaging test passes.
+- [ ] One canonical spatial toolkit path remains, without a duplicate trailing-dot toolkit directory.
+- [ ] One authoritative test run against the final tree is documented; earlier 43/49/58 counts are labelled historical where applicable.
+- [ ] Backend tests, frontend lint, TypeScript check, frontend build, spatial validator, API smoke checks and packaging checks pass, or remaining blockers are clearly listed.
+- [ ] The spatial resolution decision is evidence-based; any 10 m claim matches actual projected geometry, or the acceptance item remains open/explicitly waived.
+- [ ] Modeled heat is not presented as independently observed satellite ground truth without actual source data.
+- [ ] Spatial data provenance, cell spacing, projection, area calculations, and OSM property mappings are tested/documented.
+- [ ] The exact outgoing ZIP has been scanned and its SHA-256 recorded.
+- [ ] Final source diff has been reviewed for unrelated changes, secrets, silent fallbacks and disabled checks.
+
+**If one mandatory item is not met, mark C2 `PARTIAL / NOT CLOSED`; list each unmet item with owner, risk, file(s), reproduction steps, and next action. Do not begin C3 work.** A documented waiver is acceptable only if it explicitly identifies who must decide it and what product claim/limitation remains.
