+## 10. Final acceptance gate
+
+C2 may be marked `PASS / CLOSED` only when every mandatory criterion below is satisfied with evidence from the final source snapshot:
+
+- [ ] Area-dependent estimates use authoritative selected-area geometry or are clearly marked illustrative.
+- [ ] Area and coverage units are consistent across backend, frontend, optimizer, and export.
+- [ ] Thermal endpoints reject invalid study-area IDs with HTTP 422.
+- [ ] Grid resolution and mode parameters cannot contradict each other.
+- [ ] Either a true projected metric grid passes geometry-based 10 m tests, or the false 10 m claim is removed and the product requirement is explicitly waived.
+- [ ] OSM geometry and synthetic/modelled thermal outputs are clearly distinguished from observed data.
+- [ ] Empty optimizer results are represented truthfully.
+- [ ] Shareable project and handoff ZIPs exist, open correctly, and pass package safety checks.
+- [ ] No populated local database or secrets are shipped.
+- [ ] Final backend and frontend checks run against the final source; results reconcile with logs and JUnit.
+- [ ] Spatial validator passes.
+- [ ] SHA-256 manifest matches the actual final files.
+- [ ] No unexplained mandatory `FAIL`, `BLOCKED`, or `NOT RUN` remains.
+
+If any item fails, the overall status must remain `PARTIAL / NOT CLOSED`. List the remaining issues, do not start C3 implementation, and do not make a “complete” claim.
+
+If all mandatory criteria pass, report C2 closure with a concise evidence table and recommend that the user approve the start of C3. Do not automatically implement C3 in this task.
+
+---
+
+## 11. Execution instruction
+
+Start now by reading the audit report and JSON acceptance matrix, then inspect the repository. Execute the work in phases and make actual source changes. At each phase:
+1. state the intended minimal change;
+2. implement it;
+3. add/update regression tests;
+4. run focused checks;
+5. record evidence;
+6. continue to the next phase.
+
+Do not stop after producing a plan. Do not ask the user to repeat information already in the attached files. Ask a question only if an essential product decision cannot be inferred from the repository or audit; in particular, if the true 10 m requirement cannot be determined, present the two options and leave C2 open until the user chooses.
+
+**Final response to the user:** Summarize what changed, what passed, what failed/was blocked, link the two generated ZIPs and report, and state the C2 decision. Never claim success beyond the evidence.
